WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.850
Tell Makunouchi Ippo this...

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.850
I'm coming

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:10.360
for his belt.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.330
Wanpo! Did you come to get me?

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.030
Emotional...

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.810
I guess that describes you well.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.780
I guess everyone else sees right through me.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.720
They could tell I wasn't into hitting the mitts.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:42.720
To be honest, I don't feel right about this match.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.020
It makes sense,

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.730
since you'll have to fight against your kouhai in front of a crowd of 3,000 people.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.530
But... I have to do it.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.230
I can't just give him the belt.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.320
Will you be able to?

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:01.740
Worse than pulling punches, you might not be able to throw any at all.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.240
Do you know the meaning of the word "cannon fodder?"

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.290
Cannon fodder?

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:12.200
A fighter whose main purpose is to build up their opponent's confidence.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.260
An underdog whose sole purpose is to play the part of the loser in front of a huge crowd.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.940
Some do it because they love boxing.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.740
Some do it for the money.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.570
But they all accept the matches, knowing full well they can't win,

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.520
and end up hurting themselves.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:32.770
Occasionally, there will be an underdog who bites back and somehow emerges victorious.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.670
That is...

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.780
Hammer Nao, Yamada Naomichi.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.010
Yamada-kun is...

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.530
cannon fodder?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:47.360
Ippo-kun, do you know Hammer Nao's record?

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.520
I think it was 8 matches, 8 wins, and 5 KO's.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.990
It's a good record...

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:58.550
but did the Yamada Naomichi you knew have the talent to make it to a title match in only 8 fights?

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.470
Now that you mention it...

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:05.060
Yamada-kun wasn't in the Rookie King Tournament or the Class A Tournament.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.240
How could he have made it this far without taking the shortest path possible?

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.120
He's a no-name boxer who gets hit a lot.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.810
Most gyms were happy to send their hopefuls after him.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:19.820
No matter how bad the odds seemed, Hammer Nao always got in the ring without any hesitation.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.580
Though he would take brutal beatings, he kept on winning.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.320
It wouldn't be exaggerating to say he literally crawled his way to the top.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.640
But why?

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.430
Instead of doing something so dangerous,

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:38.330
he could have worked his way up normally, starting as a 4-rounder and gradually building his strength.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:41.340
He might have changed a lot on the surface, but not on the inside.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:46.920
He started boxing because he looked up to Makunouchi Ippo.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.990
<i>Senpai... {jama: added}</i>

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:53.230
Even now, as a boxer, he still considers you his goal.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.310
<i>Senpai! {jama: added}</i>

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.290
I don't know why he was in such a hurry,

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:58.640
<i>Senpai! {jama: added}</i>

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:05.600
but he was desperately rushing towards it and now he's reached his final goal.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.750
Final goal?

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.850
Yes.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.090
A match with Makunouchi Ippo.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.940
To him, that's a dream far greater than a world title match.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:20.170
He'll come after you with everything he has.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.100
Be careful when you face him.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.050
<i>With me as his goal...</i>

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.740
<i>He was beaten so badly and hurt so much.</i>

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.860
<i>He suffered through being treated as cannon fodder.</i>

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.750
<i>Yamada-kun...</i>

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.150
You met with Yamada-kun?

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.070
He really pissed me off.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.040
He's not our Gero-michi anymore,

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.250
so don't hold back and beat his ass!

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:52.910
Okay...

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.160
Tuck your arms in!

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.160
The geezer still won't help you with mitt hitting?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.430
Yes...

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.410
I think I really made him angry.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.570
Man, you can't even dodge that?

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.760
You really are out of it.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.020
Senpai!

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.410
Everyone's worried about you!

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.610
You seem kinda down lately.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.020
Yeah... sorry.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.170
Itagaki-kun,

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.430
do you have a goal or anything like that?

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:29.750
Well, I'd like to be a boxer who could fight on the world stage!

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:34.160
If you're gonna have a goal, then the bigger, the better!

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.030
Difficult goals help me get motivated!

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.060
W-What's wrong?

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.310
A goal...

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.770
That's right, I was chasing after Date-san and Miyata-kun.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.480
It was because of them that I've been able to make it this far.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.360
A goal has to be set high,

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:08.080
and Yamada-kun chose me as his goal.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.000
<i>To him, that's a dream far greater than a world title match.</i>

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.090
I have to answer him...

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.830
with these fists!

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:23.320
Hey, the geezer's picked up the mitts again!

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:27.340
You better not throw any more brain dead punches, got it?

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:28.740
Coach...

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:29.670
What?

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:32.750
Do you think Yamada-kun will be fine with his weight control?

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.540
It doesn't seem to be having a great effect on him.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:38.100
If anything, he's probably closer to his natural weight with all that water weight gone.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.670
I see...

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.250
How about worrying about yourself instead!?

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:44.110
Go ahead and punch!

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.330
Right...

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:46.610
If he's in good condition...

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.360
then I can relax...

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.110
and hit him with everything...

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.120
I've got!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:06.960
<i>Yamada-kun...</i>

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:10.630
<i>I'll answer your challenge,</i>

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:15.560
<i>because you took such a beating to make it to this point!</i>

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:19.930
What's wrong?

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.140
The sandbag is bouncing around!

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:26.900
What would happen if you got hit with one of those?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.080
Well, you'd be sent off to dream land with one shot!

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.940
I guess he's back in the swing of things!

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.200
I don't know about that.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.280
Ippo's completely naive.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:40.790
I don't know if he'll be able to throw these same stone cold punches when he sees Gero-michi in person.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:43.290
Right, Aoki?

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.290
Why are you so gloomy?

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.590
Forget Gero-michi, you think there's any chance he'll have any trouble hitting me?

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:51.960
Aoki! Get in the ring!

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:53.090
You're sparring with the kid!

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.030
I think he'll be able to hit you just fine.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.360
That's what I figured.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.600
<i>Is Aoki-san always the guinea pig?</i>

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.600
Not bad.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:08.390
Listen kid, Hammer Nao is an awkward fighter.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:12.610
He'll come for a close range fight, no matter what it costs him.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.360
Which means this range.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.570
You're going to be fighting at this range the entire time.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.770
I'm grateful for it.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:23.080
Normally, I have to close the distance myself, but he'll be coming to me.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.130
On the other hand, your strongest weapon, the Dempsey Roll...

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:28.830
I won't be able to use it.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:32.160
Why won't he be able to use the Dempsey Roll?

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.630
It requires a certain amount of distance in order to get the rotation started up.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:36.670
Power, speed, experience...

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:39.050
You've got all the advantages!

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.640
Face him head on as the champion!

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.280
Overwhelm him with raw strength!

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.100
Right!

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.610
He looks ready to go!

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:51.490
If he gets into the ring like this, something incredible is bound to happen.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.600
Sure looks like it.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.970
But that's only if Ippo can maintain this mindset.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:02.870
Yeah, Ippo's only seen Gero-michi in videos and pictures so far.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:04.870
When they meet face-to-face...

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.230
...those sentiments from two and a half years ago will start coming to the surface.

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:09.880
He'll be influenced by his feelings whether he wants to or not.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.490
It's not that they spent so much time together,

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:15.920
but they had a lot in common and really connected.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.300
They were more like a pair of best friends than a kouhai and senpai.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.230
When they said they'd both do their best, they really meant it.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.020
And now they're enemies, huh?

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:28.550
Whether he really considers him his enemy...

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.520
We'll find out tomorrow if he can take him on seriously.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:35.030
It'll all be clear when they meet each other at the weigh-in.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.650
<i>Senpai!</i>

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:38.260
<i>Makunouchi-senpai!</i>

00:08:56.200 --> 00:09:01.050
When I heard he was working hard in Hachinohe, I was so happy...

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:05.570
Now we're meeting him again, but as your opponent.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.640
We don't know why he wanted a match with you.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:14.690
It doesn't feel like we're going to see Yamada-kun.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:16.470
It's not Yamada-kun.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.320
Ippo-kun?

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:21.320
We're going to meet the fighter "Hammer Nao."

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.330
The Kamogawa guys have arrived.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.850
Ippo-kun, the challenger is already inside.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:31.990
I see.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.780
Both fighters meet the weight limit.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:07.840
Makunouchi,

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:13.250
any comments regarding your reunion or thoughts on the upcoming match?

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:19.350
It must be hard having to talk about how you're going to be fighting each other tomorrow.

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.800
In that case, could we get a handshake as a sign of good sportsmanship?

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:24.760
Oh, a handshake...

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:26.950
Okay.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:34.580
Hey, the champion's offering his hand, that's rude.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:37.120
Senpai...

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:41.170
I'll say this, Senpai.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.430
I owe you a lot.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.730
You taught me a lot about boxing

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.700
and now you're giving me the belt.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.710
Champion, any response to that comment?

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.970
Well, I guess...

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.250
I don't think he owes me anything.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:10:59.710
What do you mean?

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:03.720
We did train together for a while,

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.470
but...

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.460
I never taught him how to take the belt.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:10.980
So they're going to fight seriously!?

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.810
Kid, we're leaving.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:15.110
Okay! {jama: added}

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:29.010
Who gives a crap about Hammer Nao?

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:29.990
He's just some cannon fodder,

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:31.190
piece of cake!

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:34.000
I hope we get to see an awesome KO!

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:39.010
All right, I'm almost ready to go.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.420
Good luck, Aoki-san!

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.040
Don't even worry!

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.930
This guy's only ranked 10th in the Philippines.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.010
It'll be a piece of cake!

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.010
But still, no matter who it is, you should take things seriously!

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:51.210
I get it, I get it.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:54.020
I don't mean to brag, but I'm used to fighting against cannon fodder.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:55.560
<i>That's not something to brag about.</i>

00:11:55.560 --> 00:12:00.210
Aoki-sama, the underdog hunter, is gonna show you how to polish off guys who don't stand a chance!

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:02.040
<i>It just sounds like bullying the weak.</i>

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:06.920
I'm taking off, so get ready!

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:09.280
It'll be over in the first round and you're up after that!

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:10.280
Right!

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:11.290
Do your best! {jama: added}

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:13.550
We're gonna head up to the stands too.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:14.790
We'll be cheering you on!

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.720
8 matches, 8 wins, 5 KO's.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:26.590
Horizontal hooks are his speciality.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.590
Be especially careful of his left hook to the body.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.340
When I saw him yesterday I couldn't believe it was the same Yamada-kun.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:37.650
He's changed a lot in two years,

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.430
but he still thinks of me as his goal.

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:42.360
His goal, huh?

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:46.180
Over already?

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.530
That's pretty impressive, Aoki-san.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.000
What're you laying around for?

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:49.210
ONE

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.530
Looking pretty lame there, Aoki!

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.550
What the hell are you doing, dumbass!?

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:52.490
TWO

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:55.030
I thought you were an underdog hunter, doofus!

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:56.030
THREE

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:58.040
Oopsie-daisy!

00:12:58.910 --> 00:12:59.910
FOUR

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.060
He managed to land his opening shot.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:03.000
Stop the count!

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:05.510
We're just getting started, Mr. Referee!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.580
He really got you, moron!

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.510
It's because you let your guard down, idiot!

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:13.230
He rushed in to finish him!

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.230
Here it comes!

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.430
It's the Frog Punch!

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:21.830
Now the other guy is down!

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:22.980
I was waiting for that!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.610
This is one crappy match.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.490
So you <i>can</i> land a punch like that.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:28.540
He's getting up!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.090
I did it!

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:30.490
Aoki, use the Frog again!

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:31.730
I did it! I did it!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.170
Go for a Triple Cross Frog Punch!

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:33.490
Tomiko!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.490
There's no such thing!

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:39.100
The match before ours is really heating up.

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:43.330
They're knocking each other around already and Aoki's on the offensive now.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:44.690
I see,

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:46.780
so I guess there won't be an upset.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:48.760
Nao...

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:52.750
That's what eventually happens to all cannon fodder...

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:53.770
even me!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:55.570
Calm down!

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:57.030
You gotta calm down Nao!

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:58.270
Don't get nervous!

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.760
Me, the others in the gym, and everyone in the shopping district are all counting on you!

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:06.020
Do you know how happy we'd be if you brought the belt back?

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:11.890
But more importantly, we wanna see you do your best!

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.170
So just focus on the match!

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:20.080
Y-Yesterday, Makunouchi Ippo said that he never taught me how to take the belt.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.380
He was serious...

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.000
He's going to fight me seriously.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.550
I'm scared...

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.780
His punches aren't normal.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:31.560
Thinking about them hitting me was so scary that...

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.050
I couldn't sleep last night.

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.870
That's totally normal!

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.070
I know you've been playing tough this whole time!

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:38.770
It must've been hard!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:42.310
There ain't a boxer who's not afraid of Makunouchi's punches!

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:46.040
When you ignored his handshake,

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.070
I was worried that you might make him serious.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:49.270
No...

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:51.660
I'm glad he's going to take it seriously.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:53.530
If he didn't, it would be meaningless!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.520
What are you...

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:01.320
No matter what happens, I want to fight the serious Makunouchi Ippo!

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:04.970
What I'm worried about is whether or not I can withstand his punches!

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:11.090
I started boxing because I idolized Makunouchi Ippo and, 
before I knew it, I was chasing after him!

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:14.930
I didn't want to lose sight of him!

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:18.350
I thought that maybe we could meet again if I kept boxing!

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:21.920
I made my debut and knew I got stronger,

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.600
so I wanted to show my senpai that even I was able to do it!

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:27.200
You could've told him anytime!

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.370
You could've gotten in touch with him!

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.610
I'll tell him today.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:38.410
In the ring, I'll let him know everything...

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:39.870
How hard I've worked these last two years!

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.620
That I've gotten stronger!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:46.890
With every single punch, I'll let him know!

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:51.400
My style of boxing is one where I get hit a lot.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:55.570
I know that means my boxing career will be a very short one.

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:58.890
So while I'm still in my best condition, I want to show my senpai!

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:04.890
That's why you put out a challenge for the Japanese title after only eight matches.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.610
But all that ends today.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.970
I have no interest in making the world title my goal or anything like that.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:13.920
Regardless of the result, once this match is over, I won't have any regrets.

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:16.400
I'll retire.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:18.910
Nao...

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:24.630
I see...

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.930
So that's how you feel.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:29.170
I'm really sorry, Coach,

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.920
but I feel better after telling you everything.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.380
You've got nothing to apologize for!

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:36.170
Keep your head high!

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:39.800
Hold it up high and let the champion know!

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:43.180
Tell Makunouchi Ippo what you've been doing these last two years!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.100
Coach...

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.190
Right!

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.410
Winner!

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.190
In the red corner, Aoki!

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:52.350
Stop acting cool!

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:53.690
It ended up as a decision!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:57.010
I can't believe you got into a mudslinging match with some cannon fodder!

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.580
How did Aoki-san do?

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.350
Well, he <i>did</i> win.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:09.120
He didn't look like much of a hunter though.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.580
Try not to polish off anyone the way that he did. {Solo-  Polish?  TLC}

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:13.410
R-Right!

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:14.590
I'll do my best!

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:16.410
<i>I'm giving it my all!</i>

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.090
<i>That's my answer to Yamada-kun...</i>

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:22.600
<i>who made me his goal!</i>

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:27.600
And now, tonight's main event...

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:31.600
the Japanese Featherweight Title Match scheduled for 10 rounds.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.110
What's wrong, Nao?

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:42.120
<i>Do you see the stains along the hallway?</i>

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.130
<i>They're marks made from gloves.</i>

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:49.860
<i>Everybody tries to calm themselves down while hitting the wall like this. Bam! Bam!</i>

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:56.020
Calm down...

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.880
Calm down... Calm down...

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:05.610
I just have to use what I've learned these two years!

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:06.380
Hey...

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:10.890
I have to show Makunouchi-senpai what I can do at my best!

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.150
My best...

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.820
That's enough already!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.150
You're gonna hurt your hand before the match even starts!

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:23.530
I-I'm fine...

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.030
I'm fine now.

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:28.740
Listen, do you know what I want from you?

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:34.910
You might be content with being able to show Makunouchi what you can do, but I won't!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:38.940
Your conditioning and spirit are better than they've ever been!

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.630
I'm sure you're gonna fight your best match ever!

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.910
But on top of that, I'm hoping that you'll win.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.420
That you'll take the belt.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.930
That's what I want.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:55.290
And now, in the blue corner, the challenger Hammer Nao!

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:58.450
The fight between former gymmates starts now!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.710
8 matches, 8 wins, 5 KO's!

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:02.950
It's his first appearance in Korakuen Hall!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:06.020
Nao! We all came to cheer you on!

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:09.750
This might be the Champion's hometown, but you won't be left wanting for cheers!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.350
We won't let you feel like you're alone!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:12.350
Everyone...

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:14.720
Nao, you can do it!

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:15.460
Nao!

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:16.580
Take the belt!

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:18.960
Once the fight's over, you'll be the champion!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.970
Entering next is the champion, Makunouchi Ippo!

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:29.190
There are 13 dazzling KO stars marking the front of his trunks!

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:30.590
Will another star be added tonight?

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:33.420
Will he successfully defend his title once again?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:37.160
Get a load of these cheers!

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:40.980
This champion is undoubtedly popular in Korakuen Hall!

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.630
Makunouchi! {jama: added}

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.980
Don't let the challenger's gruesome mug scare you!

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:48.490
Here comes the champion, Makunouchi Ippo...

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:03.440
Both fighters,

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:06.130
to the center of the ring.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:15.350
Former senpai and kouhai now meet each other as champion and challenger!

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:19.770
There's no hint of familiarity in their eyes!

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:22.930
They're clearly meeting as enemies!

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:24.140
<i>Yamada-kun...</i>

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:26.660
Will Makunouchi Ippo overpower the challenger?

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.060
Will Hammer Nao surpass his senpai?

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:30.280
<i>Senpai...</i>

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:36.110
What drama will unfold in this tragic reunion after two and a half years!?
